 verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that destroyed the original data.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA hybrid approach is generally the most reliable and efficient.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore;", "elapsed_s": 3.777904060028959, "ttft_s": 0.6357208479894325, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 470.30400000000003, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.709333333333333, "prompt_per_second": 114.81935088793631, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3142.1130000000003, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.741047244094492, "predicted_per_second": 40.418660945675725}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.417757791267334, "end_to_end_output_tps": 33.88122037144025, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored. If the backup fails during a crisis, it is not a backup\u2014it is an archive.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundational Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your primary data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media", "elapsed_s": 3.754078848985955, "ttft_s": 0.6097739710239694, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 471.201, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.567290909090909, "prompt_per_